513 0 obj
<<
/Title (The tuple is only 16 bytes smaller here, because both hold one 8-byte pointer per item. A list header is larger \(56 vs 40 bytes\), and a list built by repeated append also over-allocates spare capacity \(roughly 12 percent\), so such a list can be noticeably bigger than the tuple. getsizeof is shallow: it does not count the 1,000,000 int objects themselves \(about 28 bytes each for large ints\), which are the same for both containers.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 449 0 R
/Prev 512 0 R
>>
