746 0 obj
<<
/Title (\(b\) Dictionary keyed by date \(for example {'2026-01-05': 12.4, ...}\). The average for a day is found by looking up the 7 date keys, each O\(1\) average. A late reading is just d[date] = value in O\(1\) with no shifting, and a missing day is detectable. The drawbacks are higher memory and the fact that slicing by position is not available, so ordered traversal needs the dates generated in order or the keys sorted \(O\(n log n\)\).)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 635 0 R
/Prev 702 0 R
/Next 766 0 R
>>
endobj
747 0 obj
