755 0 obj
<<
/Title (In [[0]*3]*3, [0]*3 is evaluated once and the outer *3 copies the reference three times, so grid[0] is grid[1] is grid[2] is True \(same id in the output\). The list comprehension runs [0]*cols once per row, creating 3 distinct lists, so each row has its own id. The inner integers 0 are immutable and shared safely, which is why only the row lists matter.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 709 0 R
/Prev 771 0 R
>>
endobj
